  "limitations": [
    "One initial baseline axiom invocation failed because the generated probe had an import after declarations. Its output and failed status/hash are retained, but its source was overwritten when corrected; the corrected baseline and final probes both passed.",
    "The final refresh borrowed eight authenticated prerequisite objects and the updated GapSource66 object, rebuilt seven gap descendants and reran gap client, focus and axiom checks. Other dependencies including RatioReparameterization and Mathlib remained precompiled; this is not a full fresh dependency closure.",
    "Target output and focused checks are warning-free; 23 split-client and 24 gap-client warnings match between baseline and final. Refreshed prerequisite GapCertificate66 and GapKernels66 emitted 26 and 13 warnings without a comparable refreshed baseline.",
    "The measured target object increases were 512 and 544 bytes. Times were single observations with concurrent processes and do not establish a general speedup.",
    "Compiled objects and overlay symlinks are excluded; drivers retain original temporary paths rather than a standalone replay environment."
  ],
  "independent_review": "Each file is byte-identical outside its generated coefficient-map region; the six original theorem signatures match. The maintained split and gap generators reproduce their outputs nonmutatingly. The original 174 per-index branches are replaced by finite-case simplification while retaining all definitions and interfaces. Seven corrected baseline and seven final checks pass, their logs are byte-identical, and 93 public axiom reports match. Ten refreshed gap-chain checks pass and their gap-client, focus and axiom output agrees with baseline. No correctness, API or generator defect was found."
